# git-secrets allowlist (repository root, read automatically by `git secrets`).
#
# These are AWS *documentation example* account IDs — not real accounts. The
# project deliberately uses them as placeholders in tests, fixtures, and docs
# (the no-private-data discipline scrubs any real id to 123456789012, the
# canonical AWS example account). Allowing them here stops git-secrets flagging
# the placeholders as if they were leaked credentials.
#
# Only specific known-fake IDs are listed — NOT a blanket [0-9]{12} — so a real
# 12-digit account id would still be caught.
123456789012
111122223333
670000000000
549999999999
